<!--
  Rendering-related edits made to a copy of the TurtleBot3 world in week 2
  (ROS Noetic + Gazebo 11), transcribed from the screenshot in
  figures/week2_optimized_world_file.png.

  How it was used:
    mkdir -p ~/turtlebot3_ws/worlds
    cp /opt/ros/noetic/share/turtlebot3_gazebo/worlds/turtlebot3_world.world \
       ~/turtlebot3_ws/worlds/my_optimized_world.world
    # then add / change the elements below inside <world name="default">

  Only the edited elements are shown. The remaining content of the world file
  (ground plane, physics block, turtlebot3_world model) comes from the
  ROBOTIS turtlebot3_simulations package (Apache-2.0) and is unchanged.
  The original world file also contains its own <scene> block; the week-2
  report notes that duplicated settings were removed, so make sure no later
  <scene> element turns shadows back on.
-->
<world name="default">

  <!-- 1. Scene: no shadows, no grid, no origin marker -->
  <scene>
    <shadows>false</shadows>
    <grid>false</grid>
    <origin_visual>false</origin_visual>
  </scene>

  <!-- 2. Main light source: stop it from casting shadows -->
  <light name="sun" type="directional">
    <cast_shadows>false</cast_shadows>
  </light>

</world>
